OTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique), which resulted in the equal distribution of both the classes (0 and 1). Used the following modules in Python-Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, matplotlib, Imbalanced-learn Logistic Regression gave AUC=0.95, but the precision was very low (0.08). So, I tried Random Forests and it gave AUC=0.94 and precision=0.85 (with 'gini' criterion) and AUC=0.92 & precision=0.83 (with 'entropy' criterion). Measured performance metrics-accuracy, precision, recall, AUC and plotted ROC curve Used the following modules in Python-Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, matplotlib, Imbalanced-learn","topics":[],"score":216224,"global_rank":256800,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":43344},{"name":"EcotopeResearch/jEplus_Modifier","owner":"EcotopeResearch","html_url":"https://github.com/EcotopeResearch/jEplus_Modifier","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"python script and text files to add multiple parameters to jEplus without getting carpal tunnel","topics":[],"score":216222,"global_rank":256801,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":43345},{"name":"momosally/python-learning","owner":"momosally","html_url":"https://github.com/momosally/python-learning","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":216222,"global_rank":256817,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":43346},{"name":"CiaranWelsh/StrokeAssessment","owner":"CiaranWelsh","html_url":"https://github.com/CiaranWelsh/StrokeAssessment","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":216222,"global_rank":256832,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":43347},{"name":"Helithumper/r-dailyprogrammer-grabber","owner":"Helithumper","html_url":"https://github.com/Helithumper/r-dailyprogrammer-grabber","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":3,"language":"Python","description":"Grabs /r/dailyprogrammer challenges daily an